155 Due Diligence before Redevelopment
Before commencement of redevelopment, the Society shall,
wherever applicable—
(a) verify the title and property records;
(b) complete conveyance or deemed conveyance;
(c) verify approved plans, Occupation Certificate, Completion
Certificate and other statutory approvals;
(d) review pending litigation or encumbrances affecting
redevelopment;
(e) update statutory records of the Society;
(f) recover outstanding dues, as far as practicable;
(g) take such further steps as may be necessary for successful
implementation of the project.
