174 Safety of Structure, Common Property and Statutory
Compliance
(a) Every Member and occupant shall use his flat, common areas
and Society property in a safe, lawful and responsible manner
and shall not undertake any act which is likely to affect—
(i) structural stability;
(ii) fire safety;
(iii) emergency access or refuge areas;
(iv) waterproofing;
(v) common services or installations;
(vi) public health or environmental safety;
(vii) rights of other Members in the common property.
(b) No person shall—
(i) carry out unauthorised construction, structural alteration or
encroachment;
(ii) damage or interfere with common property or common
installations;
(iii) obstruct passages, staircases, fire exits, refuge areas or
emergency access;
(iv) misuse lifts, electrical systems, pumps, fire-fighting systems or
other common utilities;
